From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 04:54:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] script: Render SVG text again once the web font it uses has
 loaded

usvg turns SVG text into paths when it parses the image, using the fonts that
the SVG font resolver hands it at that point. Since web fonts are loaded
lazily, the resolver often sees a face that has not been downloaded yet, asks
for it and falls back. The parsed image is cached under the element's
serialized `data:` URL, so the text kept the fallback, or was not drawn at all
when the web font was the only family, even after the font had loaded.

The SVG font resolver now records on the `FontContext` when it skipped a face
that is still unloaded or loading. When a batch of web font loads is applied
and that happened, every serialized `<svg>` element that contains text is
invalidated, which evicts its parsed and rasterized image and serializes it
again, so that it is parsed with the loaded font.

Fork note: follow-up to "fonts: Do not create fonts for web font faces that
are not loaded yet"; fold into the lazy loading patches at the next sync.

Testing: New test tests/wpt/mozilla/tests/mozilla/svg/svg-text-web-font.html,
which fails without this change.

Validation: the new reftest passes 3 of 3 runs (fails 3 of 3 without this change); `./mach test-wpt --release svg resize-observer css/css-transforms/transform-box` (1355 tests) all as expected; `css/css-fonts css/css-font-loading html/canvas/element/text` (704 tests): only font-variant-emoji-1 FAIL, which happens without an emoji font installed on plain ohos-main too. Headless screenshot of a page with SVG `<text>` in a web font Ahem: 20000 green pixels (two 100x100 squares) vs 0 before.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; designed, written and tested by the agent)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
